t_entity_availability_slot", "label": "Entity: AvailabilitySlot (bound to provider, not service)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The slot belongs to the person, not the service, so booking it for one service consumes it for every other service that provider offers - this is what prevents double-booking a human."}, {"id": "project_report_entity_booking", "label": "Entity: Booking (consumer, slot, service, status)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "project_report_entity_meeting_link", "label": "Entity: MeetingLink (booking, url, provider=Google Meet)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "project_report_entity_google_account_connection", "label": "Entity: GoogleAccountConnection (per-provider OAuth tokens)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores each provider's encrypted refresh token + googleEmail, with a nullable fallbackMeetUrl for providers who skip OAuth entirely."}, {"id": "project_report_entity_app_settings", "label": "Entity: AppSettings (single-row typed settings)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single-row typed table was chosen over a generic key/value table and over yaml-only config, because yaml cannot be written or refreshed live in production; the default is seeded from application.yaml and cached at runtime."}, {"id": "project_report_mvp_scope", "label": "MVP Scope (6 in-scope areas, payments/reviews out)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bootcamp rule of 3-5 core feature areas; payments/billing, ratings/reviews and multi-tenant orgs deliberately excluded from the MVP."}, {"id": "project_report_future_development_plan", "label": "Future Development Plan (Day 6)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "project_report_bookit_design_system", "label": "BookIt Design System (teal tokens, core components)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2-6.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Design-System-first in Claude Design (tokens + core components) so every generated screen stays consistent, then pulled into the repo one component at a time via DesignSync."}, {"id": "project_report_availability_pressure_palette", "label": "Availability-pressure palette (High/Medium/Low/None)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept visually distinct from the teal primary and reinforced with a numeric badge + opacity rather than colour alone, so it stays readable and colourblind-safe. Weekends are not special: a day is shadowed only when it has 0 available slots."}, {"id": "project_report_booking_horizon", "label": "Max booking horizon (admin-configurable, default 6 months)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 / FR-14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounds how far ahead consumers may book; enforced both in the calendar UI and in server-side booking validation so the client filter is never the only gate."}, {"id": "project_report_provider_advance_limit", "label": "Provider advance limit (ceil(horizon x 1.5), derived)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Derived rather than stored (multiplier is yaml-only, not admin-facing) so providers can pre-load availability further ahead than consumers can currently book; the rolling window makes those slots bookable as time advances."}, {"id": "project_report_slot_provider_binding_rule", "label": "Key rule: booking a slot reserves it across the provider's services", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 ERD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the slot belongs to the person and not to a service, one booking consumes that time for every service that provider offers - the core anti-double-booking invariant."}, {"id": "project_report_journey_consumer_booking", "label": "Journey: Book an appointment (Consumer)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "project_report_journey_provider_availability", "label": "Journey: Manage my availability (Provider)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "project_report_journey_admin_operate", "label": "Journey: Operate the system (Admin)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PROJECT_REPORT.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "c